# Test-run isolation, half two of two: bun loads this file natively before
# any JS runs, so its value is baked into the environment bun starts with,
# which is what a Bun.spawn call with no `env` option inherits. See
# tests/isolate-app-settings.ts for the full explanation of why this file
# exists alongside that one. Keep this value identical to that file's
# TEST_SETTINGS_GUARD constant; tests/app-settings.test.ts pins that they
# agree.
#
# A SCREEPUB_CONFIG_DIR already in the real shell environment overrides
# this (dotenv never replaces an already-set variable), so a developer
# pointing it somewhere on purpose is respected.
SCREEPUB_CONFIG_DIR=/dev/null/screepub-test-guard

# Calibre's settings folder, guarded the same way and for the same reason.
# tests/isolate-calibre-config.ts points CALIBRE_CONFIG_DIRECTORY at a
# scratch copy of the real folder for this process and for any spawn that
# passes process.env on; this is what a spawn with no env gets instead, a
# path Calibre can neither read nor create, so it fails rather than touch
# the real folder. See that file for the full explanation. Keep this value
# identical to the CALIBRE_CONFIG_GUARD constant in tools/calibre-config.ts;
# tests/calibre-config-isolation.test.ts pins that they agree.
CALIBRE_CONFIG_DIRECTORY=/dev/null/screepub-test-calibre-guard
